p.src:
The magnetic contribution to the action is $S_{\mathrm{mag}}
  =
  \frac{e}{c}
  \int_{t_i}^{t_f}A_i(\mathbf x)\dot x_i\,dt.$ Since $\dot x_i\,dt=dx_i$, it is a line integral along the particle’s path $\gamma$: $S_{\mathrm{mag}}
  =
  \frac{e}{c}\int_\gamma A_i\,dx_i
  =
  \frac{e}{c}\int_\gamma\mathbf A\cdot d\mathbf x.$ Break the path into short segments, take the component of $\mathbf A$ along each segment, multiply by the segment length, and add. That is the geometric meaning of the integral.

